MiniZinc is a free and open-source constraint modelling language. It
can model constraint satisfaction and optimization problems in a
high-level, solver-independent way, and compiles them to FlatZinc for
a wide range of solvers.

This package provides the minizinc compiler/driver (command line, the
MiniZinc IDE is not included), the MiniZinc standard library and the
libmzn library.

The Gecode backend is built in (gecode is required). Other solvers
that install a MiniZinc solver configuration in /usr/share/minizinc
are found automatically, e.g. libraries/or-tools (cp-sat). The HiGHS
and CPLEX backends are loaded at runtime if those libraries are
installed. The COIN-OR CBC backend is not built.

The tree-sitter, tree-feller and mimalloc sources that upstream
downloads at build time are included in the .info file and built
statically into libmzn.
